{title: O Holy Night}
{artist: Adolphe Adam; tr. John Sullivan Dwight}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 6/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [C]holy night, the [F]stars are brightly [C]shining
It is the [G]night of our dear [C]Saviour's birth
[C]Long lay the [F]world in sin and error [C]pining
Till [Am]He ap[Em]peared and the [F]soul felt its [G]worth
A [C]thrill of [F]hope, the weary world re[C]joices
For [Em]yonder [Am]breaks a [Dm]new and glorious [G]morn
[C]Fall on your [F]knees, O hear the angel [C]voices
O [F]night di[C]vine, O [G]night when Christ was [C]born
O [Am]night, O ho[Em]ly night, O [F]night di[G]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Led by the [F]light of Faith serenely [C]beaming
With glowing [G]hearts by His cradle we [C]stand
So [C]led by [F]light of a star sweetly [C]gleaming
Here [Am]come the [Em]wise men from [F]Orient [G]land
The [C]King of [F]kings lay thus in lowly [C]manger
In [Em]all our [Am]trials [Dm]born to be our [G]friend
He [C]knows our [F]need, to our weakness no [C]stranger
Be[F]hold your [C]King, be[G]fore Him lowly [C]bend
Be[Am]hold your [Em]King, be[F]fore Him [G]lowly [C]bend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Truly He [F]taught us to love one an[C]other
His law is [G]love and His gospel is [C]peace
[C]Chains shall He [F]break, for the slave is our [C]brother
And [Am]in His [Em]name all op[F]pression shall [G]cease
[C]Sweet hymns of [F]joy in grateful chorus [C]raise we
Let [Em]all with[Am]in us [Dm]praise His holy [G]name
[C]Christ is the [F]Lord, O praise His name for[C]ever
His [F]power and [C]glory ever[G]more pro[C]claim
His [Am]power and [Em]glory ever[F]more pro[G]claim[C]
{end_of_verse}
